WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:05.940
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing 14 incredible scenes

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:10.549
cut from Frozen 2, plus the amazing Anna and
Olaf songs that you'll wish had been in the

00:00:10.549 --> 00:00:11.549
movie.

00:00:11.549 --> 00:00:15.830
If you want to jump to any individual deleted
scenes or songs, there's timestamps in the

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:16.830
video description.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:21.539
There's an intriguing deleted scene from early
in the movie called "Elsa's Dream" which was

00:00:21.539 --> 00:00:25.109
the original inspiration for Elsa's big ballad
"Into The Unknown".

00:00:25.109 --> 00:00:29.330
The scene takes place just after the sisters
fall asleep together following their game

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:32.360
of charades;
then Anna is woken up by snowflakes falling

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:42.230
from a cloud created by Elsa's dream.

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:47.370
This deleted scene shows how Elsa's ice magic
can manifest physically even when she's sleeping,

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:51.210
and that she can unconsciously project moving
images from her dreams.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:55.340
The images of Iduna and the Enchanted Forest
from this discarded scene became the basis

00:00:55.340 --> 00:01:00.190
for the dream-like memories and visions that
appear to Elsa during Into The Unknown.

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:05.030
Elsa's dream continues and takes a nightmarish
turn as images of Arendellian soldiers appear

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:06.130
in the forest.

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:11.000
And the strong emotions this generates in
Elsa bring out more of her magic, creating

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:24.210
a mini-storm inside the bedroom.

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:28.890
In that final moment, Elsa literally freezes
the rain outside the castle into thousands

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:33.210
of ice crystals, which was where the idea
came from to fill the sky in Arendelle with

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:36.340
crystals at the end of Into The Unknown.

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:40.270
Another fascinating deleted scene from early
in the movie sees Elsa and Anna discover a

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:45.020
hidden room inside Arendelle castle, where
they uncover secret studies being carried

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:47.939
out into the origins of Elsa's powers.

00:01:47.939 --> 00:01:49.890
"Magical arts.

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:52.260
Dangers of dark magic.

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:55.200
Father was studying magic."

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:56.200
"Ooh.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:57.200
Oh!"

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.119
"He was studying me too."

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:00.119
"Wait, what?"

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:02.770
"This is some sort of journal.

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:09.220
I can find no record of a human with power
like hers but for the ancient myths with their

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:10.580
tragic fates."

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:15.569
"Wait a minute, this isn't father's handwriting,
it's mother's."

00:02:15.569 --> 00:02:19.810
If we look more closely at the journal, we
can see a page about the white gloves Elsa's

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:23.610
father gave her in the first movie in an attempt
to supress her ice magic.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.409
"The gloves will help.

00:02:25.409 --> 00:02:26.409
See?

00:02:26.409 --> 00:02:28.130
Conceal it."

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:30.849
"Don't feel it."

00:02:30.849 --> 00:02:35.239
And the journal entry which mentions "the
ancient myths with their tragic fates" helps

00:02:35.239 --> 00:02:39.840
us understand why Elsa's parents wanted to
try and contain their daughter's powers for

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:43.010
fear that her magical nature would lead her
to tragedy.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:47.540
This moment would also have set up the idea
of Elsa as a mythical being and foreshadowed

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:51.770
her fate later in the movie when she freezes
deep inside Ahtohallan.

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:56.140
The final part of the deleted scene gives
the sisters another shocking revelation:

00:02:56.140 --> 00:03:00.500
"These next pages are in English, but also..

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:01.500
Northuldrian."

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:02.500
"Northuldrian?

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:04.140
But that language is forbidden.

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:05.900
Why would mother know it?

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:08.620
Or dare use it?"

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:14.830
"Whatever evil my people did, whatever darkness
still roams our forest,

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:17.329
I can no longer turn my back on the past."

00:03:17.329 --> 00:03:22.129
This tells us that Northuldra culture was
actively suppressed inside Arendelle and that's

00:03:22.129 --> 00:03:27.430
probably why Iduna kept her research secret
including writing in her own language, and

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:31.170
perhaps why she hadn't yet told her daughters
that she was Northuldra.

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:35.849
The deleted scene helps explain just how much
Iduna and Agnarr were searching for answers

00:03:35.849 --> 00:03:40.349
about how to deal with Elsa's magic and shows
why they attempted the voyage to Ahtohallan.

00:03:40.349 --> 00:03:45.260
It also reveals how the sisters ended up with
their mother's Northuldra scarf.

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:49.980
This is also likely where Elsa and Anna would
have sung the deleted song "I Seek The Truth"

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:51.187
in which they try to understand the meaning
of the messages hidden in this secret room.

00:03:51.187 --> 00:03:55.599
A wonderful song deleted from the beginning
of the movie was a solo for Anna called "Home"

00:03:55.599 --> 00:03:57.709
in which she sings about how much she loves
Arendelle.

00:03:57.709 --> 00:03:58.709
Let's take a look.

00:03:58.709 --> 00:04:02.920
The intention behind this beautiful number
was to establish how Anna will be the perfect

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:05.269
Queen for Arendelle by the end of the film.

00:04:05.269 --> 00:04:09.090
It shows how she is completely at ease and
loves everything about her kingdom.

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:14.459
"Either way, for what it's worth, this perfect
corner of the Earth

00:04:14.459 --> 00:04:18.780
Is home
My home."

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:21.139
And it would also have highlighted just how
much Anna had to lose by her decision to destroy

00:04:21.139 --> 00:04:22.139
the dam that threatens to flood Arendelle.

00:04:22.139 --> 00:04:23.330
And it would also have highlighted just how
much Anna had to lose by her decision to destroy

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:25.370
the dam that threatens to flood Arendelle.

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:30.260
The sweetness of this song also contrasts
perfectly with her much sadder song "The Next

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:35.139
Right Thing" which she sings at her absolute
lowest after realising that both her sister

00:04:35.139 --> 00:04:36.740
and Olaf are gone.

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:41.610
"Home" would have also contrasted more with
Elsa's big number "Into The Unknown", highlighting

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:45.310
the differences between the sisters and foreshadowing
the end of the movie.

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:49.190
In other words, Anna loves her kingdom and
her place is there.

00:04:49.190 --> 00:04:50.300
"Hey, come 'ere.

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:53.620
Take this coin and go buy a custard bun for
everyone."

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:54.620
"OK."

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:59.360
Whereas Elsa is drawn by a call from afar
and her destiny lies outside Arendelle.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:03.960
Sadly, the filmmakers had to cut the song
and replace it with the ensemble number "Some

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:07.970
Things Never Change" when they realised they
still hadn't set things up sufficiently to

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:12.520
show what was at stake for Elsa, Kristoff
and Olaf when Arendelle came under threat.

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:17.130
However, they did take the overall theme of
the deleted song and one of its lyrics and

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:21.611
compressed it into the line that Anna says
to Olaf just before they sing "Some Things

00:05:21.611 --> 00:05:26.780
Never Change":
"I have you and Elsa and Kristoff and Sven...

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:30.030
and the gates are open wide...
and I'm not alone anymore."

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:35.349
"Unmeltable Me" is a great song by Olaf that
ended up being cut from the final film.

00:05:35.349 --> 00:05:39.669
It was the movie's original way to explain
why the magical snowman no longer needed the

00:05:39.669 --> 00:05:43.720
little snow flurry that Elsa gave him in the
first movie to stop him from melting.

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:46.349
"Who is present, but not liquescent?

00:05:46.349 --> 00:05:49.930
That's right, I just learned to read
And I like the big words."

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:52.979
I imagine a lot of fans would have loved to
have seen it in the movie.

00:05:52.979 --> 00:05:56.879
In the final film, this song was replaced
with the scene where Anna visits the little

00:05:56.879 --> 00:06:01.320
snowman and casually asks him about his new
"permafrost" while he basks in the warmth

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:02.500
of an autumn day.

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:08.020
There's a great shot in the first teaser trailer
for Frozen 2 of Anna grabbing Kristoff's sword

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:10.250
and attacking someone off camera.

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:14.340
That scene never made it into the final movie
because the story changed and it wasn't needed

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:15.340
any longer.

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:19.849
However, when the filmmakers discovered just
how much fans loved seeing Anna wield a sword,

00:06:19.849 --> 00:06:24.240
they made sure she had one in the movie, albeit
in a slightly different way.

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:27.919
In the final film, when the gang are scared
by the noise of approaching strangers in the

00:06:27.919 --> 00:06:33.349
forest, Anna grabs an ice sword from one of
Elsa's ice memory statues and uses it to defend

00:06:33.349 --> 00:06:37.919
the group against the Northuldra and Arendellians
who suddenly appear.

00:06:37.919 --> 00:06:42.430
Kristoff's part in Frozen 2 underwent some
major changes as the movie developed.

00:06:42.430 --> 00:06:47.139
At the beginning of the original story, Kristoff
was a lord in Arendelle, having been promoted

00:06:47.139 --> 00:06:51.590
again from his official title of "Ice Master
and Deliverer" that Elsa gave him at the end

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:52.789
of the first film.

00:06:52.789 --> 00:06:57.419
However, given Kristoff's humble origins,
he was finding it difficult fitting into Arendellian

00:06:57.419 --> 00:06:58.710
high society.

00:06:58.710 --> 00:07:03.310
And he was keeping his feelings about this
a secret, presumably to avoid upsetting Anna.

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:06.990
The truth would eventually come out though
in a deleted scene with Kristoff and the Nokk

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:08.370
water spirit.

00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:11.270
"I think he's offering you a ride."

00:07:11.270 --> 00:07:12.750
"Are you afraid?"

00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:14.159
"No, afraid of what?"

00:07:14.159 --> 00:07:17.090
"Afraid he won't see truth in your heart and
he'll drown you?"

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:18.090
"Er."

00:07:18.090 --> 00:07:19.090
"Are you?"

00:07:19.090 --> 00:07:20.090
"What?

00:07:20.090 --> 00:07:21.090
No.

00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:22.090
Course not."

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:23.750
"Then get on."

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:27.630
"See, I knew it would be fine.

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:28.630
Kristoff!"

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:29.630
"I'm OK.

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:30.630
I'm.."

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:42.780
"Except the part where his heart's full of
lies apparently."

00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:46.009
"Are you OK?

00:07:46.009 --> 00:07:47.009
Are you good?"

00:07:47.009 --> 00:07:48.009
"I'm good.

00:07:48.009 --> 00:07:49.009
Thank you."

00:07:49.009 --> 00:07:50.009
"Except you're lying about something."

00:07:50.009 --> 00:07:52.639
"I don't like fancy shoes or regal jackets."

00:07:52.639 --> 00:07:54.849
"Not a problem."

00:07:54.849 --> 00:07:56.413
"I don't like ceremonies or polite conversations."

00:07:56.413 --> 00:07:57.413
"How about ice mastering and delivering?"

00:07:57.413 --> 00:07:58.413
"No, cos it's not a thing."

00:07:58.413 --> 00:08:04.370
"Formal dinners and ballroom dancing?"

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:05.949
"No, and no."

00:08:05.949 --> 00:08:08.979
"Do you even like your life in Arendelle at
all?

00:08:08.979 --> 00:08:11.669
Just tell me the truth."

00:08:11.669 --> 00:08:14.840
"No I don't like my life in Arendelle."

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:19.169
"So, it was all a lie, all of it?

00:08:19.169 --> 00:08:20.169
"Anna, I.."

00:08:20.169 --> 00:08:22.189
"I don't think we should get married."

00:08:22.189 --> 00:08:25.860
I think this scene would have come around
the middle of the movie after the gang enter

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:27.430
the Enchanted Forest.

00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:32.020
The Nokk did appear briefly to Olaf in the
forest in the final film, and this break-up

00:08:32.020 --> 00:08:36.010
between Anna and Kristoff would have been
an alternate way to separate them.

00:08:36.010 --> 00:08:40.580
Overall, this unused scene feels just a little
too unhappy though compared to the final movie

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:44.020
where the couple are split up in the forest
more because they are a little of out of sync

00:08:44.020 --> 00:08:48.360
with each other and because Anna is focussed
on helping her sister with her quest to Ahtohallan.

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:52.930
However, there is another deleted Kristoff
and Anna scene in which he proposes to her

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:56.070
in a grand, glorious and hilarious way when
he sings to her.

00:08:56.070 --> 00:09:01.010
You can watch my full breakdown of that in
my Frozen 2 Deleted Ending video.

00:09:01.010 --> 00:09:05.610
The opening scene and prologue of Frozen 2
which tells the story of young Iduna and Agnarr

00:09:05.610 --> 00:09:09.640
and the Enchanted Forest was changed many
times during the movie's development as it

00:09:09.640 --> 00:09:13.740
had to match up with any other story changes
in the main part of the film.

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:17.540
On the Blu-ray, there's an alternate prologue
that would have shown how Iduna and Agnarr

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:20.839
escaped the fighting between the Arendellians
and the Northuldra.

00:09:20.839 --> 00:09:25.070
In this version, when the spirits are angered,
young Agnarr almost falls off a cliff before

00:09:25.070 --> 00:09:26.589
Iduna rescues him.

00:09:26.589 --> 00:09:31.020
Mattias then picks them both up and puts them
on a cart fleeing the chaos inside the forest

00:09:31.020 --> 00:09:33.000
and heading back to Arendelle.

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:37.331
In the final film, Agnarr says he never knew
who saved him that day, and instead of the

00:09:37.331 --> 00:09:41.970
deleted scene, what we get is Elsa seeing
memories of the past inside Ahtohallan and

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:46.260
learning that it was Iduna who smuggled herself
and an unconscious Agnarr on to a cart that

00:09:46.260 --> 00:09:48.040
took them out of the forest.

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:52.300
An interesting detail in this alternate prologue
is that there's a mysterious human character

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:56.519
in the forest who can either shapeshift or
moves with the appearance of a reindeer.

00:09:56.519 --> 00:10:01.089
This mystery human saves Iduna at one point
and is also attacked by Agnarr's father, the

00:10:01.089 --> 00:10:03.000
King of Arendelle.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:07.339
This Is Us star Sterling K Brown's character
Mattias also had a different storyline in

00:10:07.339 --> 00:10:09.160
earlier versions of the film.

00:10:09.160 --> 00:10:13.160
Originally, the high-ranking military man
was going to be trapped in the Enchanted Forest

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:17.910
all by himself, rather than with his fellow
Arendellians as happens in the final film.

00:10:17.910 --> 00:10:22.300
Mattias's original story would have included
him singing a song, though that ended up being

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:26.920
deleted from the movie as, ultimately, it
'didn't fit in with the story'.

00:10:26.920 --> 00:10:30.920
The trailer scene of the wind spirit Gale
uncovering young Agnarr from a bed of leaves

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:35.600
in the forest and blowing him into the air
didn't make it into the final film either.

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:39.750
The reason for that is the scene is actually
part of a test that the animators did to learn

00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:42.660
how to animate the personality of the wind
spirit.

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:46.670
The longer version of this scene is on the
Blu-ray which also shows some cute moments

00:10:46.670 --> 00:10:49.480
between young Iduna and Agnarr.

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:53.660
Another cut trailer scene shows a young Iduna
carrying a baby reindeer as the Northuldra

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:56.649
cross over the dam to greet the Arendellians.

00:10:56.649 --> 00:11:00.720
And this trailer scene of Kristoff riding
a herd of charging reindeer wasn't in the

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:02.290
final movie either.

00:11:02.290 --> 00:11:06.600
The trailer scene of Olaf standing next to
Elsa as she tries to put out the fires in

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:12.070
the forest was altered for the final movie
where Elsa fights the fire spirit alone.

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:16.000
And in another change from the trailers, this
shot of Queen Iduna looking out of the bedroom

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:20.380
window at the Northern Lights was replaced
with Iduna carrying young Elsa to look out

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:21.740
of the window together.

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:26.610
There's also a much darker original ending
to Frozen 2 in which Disney almost killed

00:11:26.610 --> 00:11:28.800
off Elsa and destroyed Arendelle.

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:33.480
To learn all about that as well as Kristoff's
alternate proposal to Anna, tap here or follow

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:35.300
the link in the video description.

00:11:35.300 --> 00:11:39.510
And if you want to see all the deleted scenes
in full, check out the Blu-ray – I've added

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:41.120
links to that in the description.

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:45.279
So, which of these deleted scenes and songs
do you wish had been in the movie and which

00:11:45.279 --> 00:11:46.850
are you glad were cut?

